      "FacilityID": 1000120742,
      "SummaryText": "Executive Summary for 2025 RMP Submittal\n\nAccidental Release Prevention and Emergency Response Policies\n\nTextile Rubber & Chemical Company (TRCC) makes every effort to prevent the accidental release of all chemicals, with special emphasis on the chemicals subject to the EPA's Risk Management Program and OSHA's Process Safety Management program.\n\nTRCC's environmental, health, and safety programs are a top priority for all levels of TRCC management.\n\nTRCC Facility & Regulated Substances\n\nTRCC is a specialty chemical manufacturer operating both chemical reaction processes and\nchemical blending processes. TRCC uses the following RMP regulated substances: carbon disulfide (75-15-0); dimethylamine (124-40-3); and monomethylamine (74-89-5). These chemicals are stored in bulk quantities in stationary storage tanks. TRCC is located in Dalton, Georgia.\n\nGeneral Accidental Release Prevention Program and Chemical-Specific Prevention Steps\n\nTRCC complies with both the EPA's Risk Management Program and OSHA's Process Safety\nManagement. Both of these regulatory programs include detailed requirements addressing areas such as process safety information, hazard assessment, mechanical integrity, contractor safety, operating procedures, management of change, and incident investigation. As part of implementing these programs, TRCC has developed a PSM/RMP Program Manual that provides written guidance for following all of these regulatory requirements. In addition, the Program Manual includes working logs to help TRCC management track implementation of the programs.\n\nFive-Year Accident History\n\nThere have been no reportable accidents in the past 5 years."
    }
